// ABOUTME: Base signing config for the app target, checked in with no account in it.
// ABOUTME: A device build reads DEVELOPMENT_TEAM from an untracked Signing.xcconfig.local.

// Simulator builds need nothing here: `make build` passes CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
// and runs with no team and no Apple account. This file exists for device and
// release builds, which do need a signing identity.
//
// To build on a device, create Signing.xcconfig.local next to this file with
// your ten-character Apple Developer Team ID:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//
// That file is gitignored (`*.xcconfig.local`), so your account never lands in
// the repo. The release path takes the same value from the environment instead
// (see .env.example), so automation and the IDE stay consistent.
//
// A contributor on a different team also needs their own PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER
// and must register the `group.net.cotellese.mindgrapes` App Group under their
// account; set the bundle id in the same local file. The maintainer's team owns
// the canonical ids, so this is only for third-party device builds.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// The `?` makes the include optional: a fresh clone with no local file still
// generates and builds for the simulator.
#include? "Signing.xcconfig.local"
